aragraph"}],"runtimePreview":null,"media":null},{"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Our simple case only needs a "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for the duration. In a real reminder app, a Date type would be more appropriate."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","code":"1-2-3.swift","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Define stored properties for the text of the Reminder, and a value for how long before the reminder gets sent."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s best practice when dealing with values that represent Time to specify the units in the documentation for the property."}]},{"type":"step","caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can use the Command-Option-Slash ( ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"⌘-⌥-\/","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" ) hotkey to auto-generate documentation stubs for any symbol in your code."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a documentation comment for our duration specifying the unit of time being measured."}]}],"code":"1-2-3-comment.swift","runtimePreview":null,"media":null},{"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Define a stored property to hold a collection of strings to act as tags for the reminder. This allows users to more easily filter what reminders will show."}]}],"media":null,"runtimePreview":null,"code":"1-2-4.swift","caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Knowing that tags should be unique strings helps with deciding that this collection should be a Set of Strings. There would be no reason for a Reminder to have the same tag set twice!"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"caption":[],"media":null,"code":"1-2-5.swift","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Finally, make it so that if your Reminder 